 "capitulo": "Why Greenland, Why Now",
 "visual": "Rare earths icon in southern Greenland. China flag, \"90%\".",
 "texto": "Under that ground are some of the largest deposits of rare earth elements in the world. The metals inside your phone, your electric car, and a fighter jet. Right now, China processes around ninety percent of them. Greenland could be one way to break that grip. And America is not the only one looking. In 2018, a Chinese state-owned company bid to build airports in Greenland. Denmark stepped in and paid for them itself.",
